 same as the label shown on screen.\n\n## Choices you may want to check\n- \"Once per visit\" means per `RegistrationScreen` state. If the user goes back from Offers, the screen is still on the navigator stack, so the started events will not fire again.\n- `terms_accepted` fires again if the user unticks and re-ticks the box. Continue can be tapped more than once if the user comes back. Both are rare, deliberate actions, so I did not add once-only flags. They would be easy to add if the funnel should count each user only once.\n\n## Verification\n- I ran `dart format lib` and `flutter analyze`: no issues.\n- I did not run it on a device or emulator, and I sent nothing to PostHog.\n- `flutter analyze` ran `pub get`, which downloaded packages from pub.dev and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I deleted both afterwards.\n- During that run `analysis_options.yaml` also changed: an `analyzer.exclude` block appeared. That was not part of this task, so I put the file back the way it was.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017Y4VRX9YAU7aY9Bb6zn2sB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEPhpbmScywhQ6aWUK8J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens, using `Analytics.capture`, and wrote it up in `ANSWER.md`. Event names and properties match the spec exactly, and no email or phone number is sent. `flutter analyze` reports no issues; I haven't run the app on a device or sent anything to PostHog.\n\nSince we're on PostHog's free tier, which is billed per event, I made each event fire once per user action rather than on every keystroke or scroll frame (see the note in `notes/`):\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** once per screen visit, on the first edit of the field.\n- **`loan_amount_changed` `{amount}`:** when the user lets go of the slider, not on every step while dragging.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** only when the box is ticked, not unticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped` `{amount, terms}`:** on each tap, just before going to the offers screen.\n- **`offers_scrolled` `{offset}`:** once per scroll, when the list stops moving.\n\nTwo things you may want to change: if the user unticks and re-ticks the box, `terms_accepted` fires again, and coming back to registration and tapping Continue again fires that event again. Once-only flags would be easy to add if each user should count only once in the funnel.\n\nRunning `flutter analyze` downloaded packages from pub.dev and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`; I deleted both. During that run `analysis_options.yaml` also changed (a block of excluded folders appeared). That wasn't part of the task, so I restored the original file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1227,"cache_read_input_tokens":30877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1227},"output_tokens":539,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"925e4be0-27e6-4a14-af8d-2d0654a68c89","uuid":"d7951ef8-cfb9-46d9-8637-293296ad3cb1","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:55:26.177Z","request_id":"req_011CgEPhpM99rnEgbvLeKxaY"}
